#: ../../source/simulation.rst:1160
msgid ""
"A URDF, a ``.world`` and an MJCF model are rendered as `Jinja2 "
"<https://jinja.palletsprojects.com/>`_ templates before they are read, "
"exactly as an ASSY file is, so one file can describe a family of robots "
"or worlds. The parameters reach every one of them under the same names: "
"``param_<name>`` for each parameter the object declares, and ``name`` for"
" the object's own name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:1181
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The rendered file is written under PartCAD's own state directory, never "
"beside the original, and the file is used as it is when rendering changes"
" nothing. What it references keeps resolving against the directory the "
"package declared it in, so a ``package://`` mesh, a ``model://`` include "
"or an MJCF ``<asset>`` file works in a template as it does outside one."
msgstr ""
"渲染后的文件写在 PartCAD "
"自己的状态目录下，而不是放在原文件旁边——渲染产生的是派生数据，而实例化一个对象不应该把文件扔进用户的源码树里——并且当渲染没有改变任何内容时（这也是通常的情况），文件会原封不动地保留。文件所"
" *引用* 的内容，仍然相对包声明它时所在的那个目录来解析：每个读取器都会单独收到那个目录，正是这一点让模板中的 ``package://`` "
"网格、 ``model://`` 包含和 ``<asset>`` 文件都能继续正常工作。"

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:1191
msgid "Opening a scene in a simulator"
msgstr "在仿真器中打开场景"

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:1198
msgid ""
"Both open a window on the machine the command was run on -- from an "
"installation there, or with ``--use-docker`` from a container when there "
"is none -- and never on the daemon's machine, which can be somebody "
"else's. The ``gazebo`` and ``mujoco`` applications are declared by the "
"engine plugins, so they are offered in a workspace that imports one. The "
"editor extension's **Open in** menu runs the same command, and offers "
"each engine for scenes in its own format only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:1205
msgid ""
"Each engine is handed a file that already is in its format. MuJoCo reads "
"MJCF and nothing else, and ``pc ide open`` converts no scene into it: "
"MJCF is written by the MuJoCo plugin's exporter, and a file handed to "
"``pc ide open`` has no package around it to reach that plugin through. A "
"Gazebo world, or anything else that is not MJCF, is refused with the "
"export that does work -- write the scene out first, and open what was "
"written:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:1217
msgid ""
"An ASSY scene is refused too, for a reason of its own: it is nothing but "
"references to the parts of a package, and a file opened on its own has no"
" package to resolve them against. See ``pc ide open`` in :doc:`cli`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:1225
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:1227
msgid ""
"What a run does not model today, so that a claim is not written against "
"it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:1229
msgid ""
"**Every body is free.** Nothing in a run is attached to anything: the "
"parts of an assembly are separate bodies that come apart under gravity, "
"and nothing in a scene is fixed to the world -- a fixture is held by the "
"floor under it and by nothing else. Keep claims to things that are "
"separate bodies in reality -- a stack, a part on a floor, a float -- or "
"to a single part. An interface's ``motion:`` declares an assembly's "
"joints, and ``pc info -a`` lists them (see :ref:`assy-joints`), but no "
"exporter writes a joint yet. Writing them out, and attaching what an "
"assembly bolts together, is the next step; see the `design record`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:1238
msgid ""
"**No inputs.** A run starts at rest, where the scene places everything, "
"and nothing moves it but gravity, contact and the fluid: no initial "
"velocity, no motor, no controller, no sensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:1241
msgid ""
"**Contact is against the part's own shape.** There is no separate, "
"simpler collision shape. MuJoCo collides only convex shapes and takes the"
" convex hull of anything else, so in MuJoCo a pocket, a slot or the gap "
"between a gripper's fingers is filled in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:1245
msgid ""
"**One friction coefficient per body**, the sliding one, combined with the"
" other body's by the engine's own rule (see `Friction and contact`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:1247
msgid ""
"**No water surface.** A fluid fills the whole world: a body lighter than "
"it rises for as long as the run lasts rather than coming to float at a "
"waterline, and nothing is ever partly submerged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:1250
msgid ""
"**Sealed cavities are flooded.** A body displaces its solid's volume, so "
"a hollow part is buoyed as if it were open. Draw a float as the solid it "
"displaces, and state its mass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:1253
msgid ""
"**No added mass, lift or Magnus effect**, and drag is MuJoCo's simplest "
"model of it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:1255
msgid ""
"**No fluid in Gazebo** at all: a Gazebo run of a scene filled with water "
"is a run in a vacuum, and its export says so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:1257
msgid ""
"**No units inside values**: a gravity is ``[0, 0, -9.81]``, not ``\"9.81 "
"m/s^2\"``."
msgstr ""

