#~ msgid ""
#~ "That is the same rule the "
#~ "simulator itself follows, and for the"
#~ " same reason. Reading a format, "
#~ "writing it, launching the application on"
#~ " it and running a physics step "
#~ "with it are one body of knowledge"
#~ " about one engine; PartCAD ships the"
#~ " *concept* -- the ``import:`` and "
#~ "``export:`` sections, the sandbox, the "
#~ "``simulation:`` plugin protocol, the ``open:``"
#~ " entry -- and the engine's package"
#~ " supplies the knowledge. Each of "
#~ "those two packages declares all four "
#~ "for its own format, so importing "
#~ "it is what makes the type, the "
#~ "exporter, ``pc sim`` and ``pc ide "
#~ "open --with`` all work at once."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "这与仿真器本身所遵循的是同一条规则，理由也相同。读取一种格式、写出这种格式、用它启动应用程序、以及用它运行一步物理计算，属于关于同一个引擎的同一套知识；PartCAD"
#~ " 提供的是 *概念* —— ``import:`` 和 "
#~ "``export:`` 小节、沙箱、 ``simulation:`` 插件协议、 "
#~ "``open:`` 条目——而知识由该引擎的包来提供。上述两个包各自为自己的格式声明了全部这四项，因此只要导入它，类型、导出器、"
#~ " ``pc sim`` 和 ``pc ide open "
#~ "--with`` 就会同时可用。"

#~ msgid "A package that uses one imports it and names the type through it:"
#~ msgstr "用到某种格式的包会导入对应的插件包，并通过它来命名该类型："

#~ msgid ""
#~ "A bare ``type: world`` resolves to "
#~ "nothing and says so. So does ``pc"
#~ " export -t mjcf``: nothing in "
#~ "``//builtin/export`` writes either format, and"
#~ " the qualified spelling is what "
#~ "reaches the package that does."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "光写 ``type: world`` 什么也解析不到，而且它会明确说出来。 ``pc "
#~ "export -t mjcf`` 也一样： ``//builtin/export`` "
#~ "中没有任何东西能写出这两种格式，只有带限定前缀的写法才能到达真正能写的那个包。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "What the readers preserve and what "
#~ "they cannot is documented in those "
#~ "repositories, beside the code -- "
#~ "including the parts of MJCF that "
#~ "are easy to get wrong (angles are"
#~ " degrees by default, an orientation "
#~ "has five spellings, and a box's "
#~ "``size`` is its half-extents), and "
#~ "the export parameters a simulation needs"
#~ " that a scene never states "
#~ "(``static``, ``flatten``, ``light``, "
#~ "``ground_plane``, ``sun``). The two readers"
#~ " are best-effort in exactly the "
#~ "way the URDF reader above is: what"
#~ " a static arrangement cannot hold is"
#~ " counted and reported rather than "
#~ "passed over, and ``pc info`` lists "
#~ "it."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "这两个读取器保留了什么、不能保留什么，都记录在那两个仓库里、紧挨着代码——其中也包括 MJCF "
#~ "中容易弄错的部分（角度默认以度为单位，一个朝向有五种写法，而盒体的 ``size`` "
#~ "指的是它的半边长），以及仿真所需、而场景从不声明的那些导出参数（ ``static`` 、 "
#~ "``flatten`` 、 ``light`` 、 ``ground_plane`` "
#~ "、 ``sun`` ）。这两个读取器都是尽力而为的，方式与上文的 URDF "
#~ "读取器完全一样：静态布置承载不了的内容会被计数并报告，而不是被略过，而且 ``pc info`` "
#~ "会把它们列出来。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "One consequence is worth stating because"
#~ " it is a change and not an "
#~ "oversight: ``pc ide open --with mujoco``"
#~ " no longer converts a scene into "
#~ "MJCF. It opens a file that already"
#~ " is one -- the application's "
#~ "``open:`` entry names the extensions its"
#~ " format is stored in -- and "
#~ "refuses anything else with the export"
#~ " that does work. An ad-hoc "
#~ "conversion has a throwaway package "
#~ "around the file and no dependency "
#~ "on either plugin, so it cannot run"
#~ " the exporter that would be needed;"
#~ " see :doc:`cli`."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "有一个后果值得说明，因为它是一处有意的改动而不是疏漏： ``pc ide open "
#~ "--with mujoco`` 不再把场景转换成 MJCF。它打开的是本身已经是 MJCF"
#~ " 的文件——应用程序的 ``open:`` "
#~ "条目列出了它的格式所使用的扩展名——而对其他任何文件都会拒绝，并指出真正可用的那种导出方式。临时转换在文件外面只套了一个一次性的包，对这两个插件都没有依赖，因此它无法运行所需要的那个导出器；参见"
#~ " :doc:`cli` 。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "An ASSY file has always been "
#~ "rendered as a `Jinja2 "
#~ "<https://jinja.palletsprojects.com/>`_ template before "
#~ "it is parsed, which is what lets"
#~ " one file describe a family of "
#~ "assemblies. A URDF, a ``.world`` and "
#~ "an MJCF model are declared exactly "
#~ "the same way and were not, so "
#~ "a package could parameterize one kind"
#~ " of arrangement and not the other "
#~ "three. All four share one implementation"
#~ " now, and the parameters reach every"
#~ " one of them under the same "
#~ "names: ``param_<name>`` for each declared "
#~ "parameter, and ``name`` for the object's"
#~ " own."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "ASSY 文件在被解析之前，一直都会先作为 `Jinja2 "
#~ "<https://jinja.palletsprojects.com/>`_ "
#~ "模板渲染，正是这一点让一个文件能够描述一族装配体。URDF、 ``.world`` 和 MJCF "
#~ "模型的声明方式完全相同，却没有这样处理，于是一个包能把其中一类布置参数化，对另外三类却无能为力。现在这四者共用同一套实现，参数也以相同的名字送达其中每一个："
#~ " ``param_<name>`` 对应每个已声明的参数， ``name`` 对应对象自身的名字。"

#~ msgid "``scene:``"
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The scene the object is placed in,"
#~ " by full path. The object's own "
#~ "full path is assigned to that "
#~ "scene's ``subject`` parameter -- "
#~ "unconditionally, and whatever else the "
#~ "entry says -- which is what lets"
#~ " one scene serve every object that"
#~ " names it. Nothing special is "
#~ "declared for it: a simulation scene "
#~ "is an ordinary scene with an "
#~ "ordinary parameter, and a Jinja2 "
#~ "template is what places the subject."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "对象被放入的场景，用完整路径表示。对象自身的完整路径会被赋给该场景的 ``subject`` "
#~ "参数——无条件地，无论条目中还写了什么——正是这一点让一个场景可以服务于所有指名它的对象。为此不需要声明任何特殊的东西：仿真场景就是一个带普通参数的普通场景，而放置主体的则是一个"
#~ " Jinja2 模板。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The default is ``//builtin/scene:subject``, an"
#~ " empty world holding the subject and"
#~ " nothing else. A package that needs"
#~ " more -- a fixture to drop the"
#~ " part onto, a conveyor to push "
#~ "it along, a tank of water to "
#~ "sink it in -- writes a scene "
#~ "of its own. The scene is also "
#~ "what says the gravity the run is"
#~ " under and the fluid it is "
#~ "filled with; see `Gravity, and the "
#~ "fluid a scene is filled with`_."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "默认值是 ``//builtin/scene:subject`` "
#~ "，一个只装着主体、别无他物的空世界。需要更多内容的包——比如一个用来让零件落下的夹具，或者一条把它推着走的传送带——会自己写一个场景。"

