#~ msgid "2. Physical properties a part does not have to state"
#~ msgstr "2. 零件不必声明的物理属性"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "A part's ``physics:`` section already "
#~ "holds the modelled properties - "
#~ "``mass``, ``centerOfMass``, ``inertia``, "
#~ "``friction``, the contact parameters - "
#~ "each with a PartCAD name and a "
#~ "PartCAD unit. What it does not do"
#~ " is *derive* any of them, check "
#~ "any of them, or distinguish a "
#~ "measured value from a guess. Three "
#~ "additions, in increasing order of how"
#~ " much they are worth:"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "零件的 ``physics:`` 小节已经持有建模后的各项属性—— ``mass`` 、"
#~ " ``centerOfMass`` 、 ``inertia`` 、 "
#~ "``friction`` 以及接触参数——每一项都有 PartCAD 的名字和 "
#~ "PartCAD 的单位。它没有做的是：*推导* "
#~ "其中任何一项、校验其中任何一项，或者区分实测值与猜测值。下面三项补充，按价值从低到高排列："

#~ msgid ""
#~ "**Derivation** - *done*. With a material"
#~ " behind it (item 1), a part "
#~ "that states no ``mass`` has one: "
#~ "the solid's volume times the material's"
#~ " density. The same for ``centerOfMass``,"
#~ " ``inertia`` and ``friction``. The derived"
#~ " values are cached under the part's"
#~ " key and what they were derived "
#~ "from, so an edit to the CAD "
#~ "or to the material invalidates them; "
#~ "``pc info`` shows each value and "
#~ "where it came from, and every "
#~ "exporter is handed the same values "
#~ "instead of working its own out. "
#~ "See `Writing a URDF`_."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "**Provenance.** A declared value should "
#~ "say why it exists, since \"measured "
#~ "on the bench\" and \"copied from a"
#~ " vendor datasheet\" and \"invented so "
#~ "the simulation would load\" are not "
#~ "the same claim:"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "**来源。** "
#~ "声明出来的值应当说明它为什么存在，因为“在工作台上实测得到”“从供应商数据表上抄来”和“为了让仿真能加载而编出来”并不是同一种主张："

#~ msgid ""
#~ "**Checking.** ``pc lint`` should flag "
#~ "the classic defects, all of which "
#~ "are common in published URDFs and "
#~ "all of which load without complaint: "
#~ "zero mass, an inertia tensor that "
#~ "is not positive definite, one that "
#~ "violates the triangle inequality, and a"
#~ " declared mass that disagrees with "
#~ "volume times density by more than "
#~ "a tolerance."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "**校验。** ``pc lint`` 应当标出那些经典缺陷，它们在已发布的 URDF"
#~ " 中都很常见，而且加载时都不会报错：零质量、非正定的惯性张量、违反三角不等式的惯性张量，以及与体积乘密度之差超出容差的已声明质量。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Anisotropic friction is the one property"
#~ " that needs more structure than it"
#~ " has today: "
#~ "``friction``/``friction2``/``frictionDirection`` is ODE's"
#~ " shape of it, kept because it "
#~ "is what URDF states. A modelled "
#~ "version would be a static and a"
#~ " dynamic coefficient with an optional "
#~ "anisotropy, and the URDF exporter would"
#~ " flatten it on the way out."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "各向异性摩擦是唯一一项需要比现在更多结构的属性： ``friction`` / "
#~ "``friction2`` / ``frictionDirection`` 是 ODE"
#~ " 给它的形状，之所以保留下来，是因为 URDF "
#~ "就是这么表述的。建模之后的版本应当是一个静摩擦系数和一个动摩擦系数，外加可选的各向异性，而 URDF "
#~ "导出器会在写出时把它压平。"

#~ msgid "3. Collision geometry"
#~ msgstr "3. 碰撞几何体"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "A URDF's collision geometry is not "
#~ "lost today - a link that states"
#~ " both shapes is built from the "
#~ "collision one and the visual one "
#~ "becomes a part of its own - "
#~ "but the *relation* between the two "
#~ "is: they are two parts that happen"
#~ " to be named alike, and nothing "
#~ "says one is the simplified stand-"
#~ "in for the other. A part should"
#~ " be able to say it:"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "URDF "
#~ "的碰撞几何体今天并没有丢失——同时声明了两种形状的连杆由碰撞形状构建，而视觉形状会成为一个独立的零件——丢失的是两者之间的 "
#~ "*关系* ：它们只是恰好名字相似的两个零件，没有任何东西说明其中一个是另一个的简化替身。零件应当能够说出这一点："

#~ msgid ""
#~ "``convexHull`` and ``convexDecomposition`` are "
#~ "computed in a sandbox and cached "
#~ "like any derived shape; ``part`` points"
#~ " at another PartCAD part, which is"
#~ " how a hand-simplified collision "
#~ "shape gets version-controlled next to"
#~ " the real one - and is exactly"
#~ " what a URDF import would then "
#~ "produce instead of a part with a"
#~ " suggestive name; ``primitive`` fits a "
#~ "box/cylinder/sphere/capsule to the geometry."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "``convexHull`` 和 ``convexDecomposition`` "
#~ "在沙箱中计算，并像其他派生形状一样被缓存； ``part`` 指向另一个 PartCAD "
#~ "零件，手工简化出来的碰撞形状正是靠它与真实形状并排接受版本管理——而届时 URDF "
#~ "导入产出的也正是这种关系，而不是一个只靠名字暗示的零件； ``primitive`` "
#~ "则为几何体拟合一个盒/圆柱/球/胶囊。"

#~ msgid "4. Named frames"
#~ msgstr "4. 具名坐标系"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Frames are the attachment points for "
#~ "sensors, joints and grasp poses, and "
#~ "they are what an exporter needs to"
#~ " write ``<frame>`` or a sensor's "
#~ "``<origin>``. PartCAD's ``interfaces`` and "
#~ "``ports`` already describe named, located "
#~ "features on a part; frames should "
#~ "be the same mechanism, not a "
#~ "parallel one."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "坐标系是传感器、关节和抓取位姿的附着点，导出器也正是靠它们才能写出 ``<frame>`` 或者传感器的 "
#~ "``<origin>`` 。PartCAD 的 ``interfaces`` 和 "
#~ "``ports`` 本来就在描述零件上具名且有确定位置的特征；坐标系应当复用同一套机制，而不是另起一套。"

#~ msgid "5. Kinematics: a configuration, not a joint section"
#~ msgstr "5. 运动学：一个配置，而不是一个关节小节"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The obvious proposal here used to "
#~ "be a ``joint:`` form for an ASSY"
#~ " node, next to ``location:`` and "
#~ "``connect:``. Building the URDF mapping "
#~ "above argues against it. A joint "
#~ "is not a third way to place "
#~ "a part - it is what a "
#~ "``connect:`` *already is*, plus a value."
#~ " An interface says what freedom of"
#~ " movement it allows (``motion:``, "
#~ "``parameters:``); a connection says which "
#~ "two things are joined and, optionally,"
#~ " at what value (``toParams:``). Adding "
#~ "a parallel ``joint:`` section would "
#~ "restate the interface's own description "
#~ "at every use site, which is the"
#~ " duplication the rest of PartCAD "
#~ "exists to remove."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "这里显而易见的提案曾经是：给 ASSY 节点加一种 ``joint:`` 形式，与 "
#~ "``location:`` 和 ``connect:`` 并列。而上面构建 URDF "
#~ "映射的经历否定了这个想法。关节并不是放置零件的第三种方式——它就是 ``connect:`` *本来就是* "
#~ "的那个东西，再加上一个值。接口说明它允许哪些运动自由度（ ``motion:`` 、 "
#~ "``parameters:`` ）；连接说明哪两样东西被连在一起，以及可选地，连接在哪个值上（ "
#~ "``toParams:`` ）。再加一个并行的 ``joint:`` "
#~ "小节，等于在每个使用处重复一遍接口自己的描述，而这正是 PartCAD 其余部分所要消除的那种重复。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "What is actually missing is one "
#~ "level up: the assembly has no way"
#~ " to name a *configuration*."
#~ msgstr "真正缺失的东西在上一层：装配体没有办法为一个 *配置* 命名。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "with the connections referring to the"
#~ " configuration rather than carrying a "
#~ "literal:"
#~ msgstr "各个连接引用这个配置，而不是直接携带一个字面值："

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Everything that exists today - a "
#~ "tree of rigid placements - is what"
#~ " you get by evaluating a "
#~ "configuration, so no consumer of the "
#~ "representation has to change. But ``pc"
#~ " ide view 'robot;configuration=stowed'`` becomes"
#~ " meaningful through the parameter machinery"
#~ " ASSY files already have, and an "
#~ "exporter gains something to write a "
#~ "joint *state* from."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "今天已有的一切——一棵刚性位置构成的树——正是对某个配置求值之后得到的结果，因此这套表示形式的消费方一个都不需要改动。但 "
#~ "``pc ide view 'robot;configuration=stowed'`` "
#~ "会借助 ASSY 文件早已具备的参数机制变得有意义，而导出器也终于有东西可以用来写出关节的 *状态*"
#~ " 。"

#~ msgid "Two things this still needs, which the URDF work did not:"
#~ msgstr "这件事还需要两样东西，而 URDF 的工作并不需要它们："

#~ msgid ""
#~ "**A joint identity.** ``toInstance: "
#~ "shoulder_pan`` names the joint today "
#~ "only by convention. A configuration has"
#~ " to address it, so the instance "
#~ "name has to become the joint's "
#~ "name in earnest."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "**关节的身份。** ``toInstance: shoulder_pan`` "
#~ "今天只是按约定给关节命名。配置必须能够寻址到它，所以实例名必须真正成为关节的名字。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "**Loops.** A four-bar linkage is a"
#~ " connection whose child is already "
#~ "placed. PartCAD's tree cannot express it"
#~ " and neither can URDF; SDF can. "
#~ "Until then the honest behaviour is "
#~ "to detect it and say so."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "**闭环。** 四连杆机构是一种子节点已经被放置过的连接。PartCAD 的树无法表达它，URDF "
#~ "也不行；SDF 可以。在那之前，诚实的做法是检测出这种情况并明确指出来。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "There remains a genuinely attractive "
#~ "case for *deriving* joints from the "
#~ "existing interface library: a bearing "
#~ "bore is revolute about its own "
#~ "axis and a linear rail is "
#~ "prismatic along its own, so an "
#~ "interface that says so once gives "
#~ "every ``connect:`` that uses it a "
#~ "joint for free. That is the same"
#~ " ``motion:`` section the URDF conversion"
#~ " writes, applied to hand-authored "
#~ "interfaces instead of generated ones -"
#~ " which is why ``motion:`` belongs on"
#~ " the interface and not on the "
#~ "connection."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "从现有的接口库中 *推导* "
#~ "出关节，仍然是一个确实很有吸引力的方向：轴承孔绕自己的轴是旋转关节，直线导轨沿自己的轴是移动关节，所以接口只要说明一次，用到它的每一个"
#~ " ``connect:`` 都能免费得到一个关节。这与 URDF 转换所写出的是同一个 "
#~ "``motion:`` 小节，只不过作用于手工编写的接口而不是生成出来的接口——这也正是 ``motion:``"
#~ " 属于接口而不属于连接的原因。"

